between the wave's row position and the filled area's row position. I'm investigating why certain peaks and troughs are empty.\n\n\n\n**Unveiling the Cyclicity**\n\nI've made a crucial discovery: the filling pattern occurs every six columns, directly related to the wave's peaks and troughs, which occur every four columns. Columns 0, 6, 12, etc., follow an alternating fill behavior: peak fills below, trough fills above. I now see a periodicity.\n\n\n",
